<title>INDIA: India soybean steady, oil improved, meal down.</title>
<headline>India soybean steady, oil improved, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets and plant delivery condition on Tuesday, dealers said. Trading was dull and the undertone was steady. Arrivals were around 1,000 tonnes in the markets of central India.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices rose on better demand in local markets. Soyoil solvent was up by 100 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined was up by 300 rupees per tonne. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly down on limited exports demand. Soymeal yellow was $304-305 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $115 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 3,950-4,000 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition Business volumes and the undertone were steady.</p>
